                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Fox & Flock is a neat little board game. Something you play for a half hour to kill some time. Sadly, it's very light on features, almost feeling like a demo for a full featured game. But for under $2.00 I *really* can't complain. Overall, I really enjoyed it and I hope the creators decide to make a chess game with the same aesthetics.\n\nThe Good:\n++Fun game!\n++Fantastic art style\n++Fitting classical soundtrack\n+Narrator is quite entertaining\n+Local Multiplayer\n+Steam Cards\n\nThe Bad:\n-No online play\n-Story mode is short (about 20 minutes; I guess you can think of it as a tutorial)\n-Lack of game modes\n\nThe Ugly (which hopefully get patched) :\n---Questionable AI (Dumb moves, or the AI just repeats the same two moves over and over, really dragging down the flow of the game)\n---Game breaking glitches, requiring game restart\n---Inability to use Steam overlay or take screenshots",
